WEBVTT

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.410
An Incomplete Map

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.410
An Incomplete Map

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.410
An Incomplete Map

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.410
An Incomplete Map

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.410
An Incomplete Map

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.410
An Incomplete Map

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.410
An Incomplete Map

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.250
Hey, Gerald.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.510
These two have stopped moving.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.930
They're the ones who will fail.
Never take your eyes off them.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.970
Forgive me.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.850
Perhaps we should send Edward a message.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:03.940
Aileen.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.400
Yes, ma'am,

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.510
Must they send these inane messages?

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:37.140
And can't these soot pigeons
deliver them quietly?

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.760
Come look at this! Shaun is going down!

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.140
What?!

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.200
Oh, it was just a pit trap.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.740
That fool!

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:05.580
Neglecting to show elevation
on the map was by design?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.330
As expected, it seems
Lou will arrive first.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.540
Perhaps not.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.300
It's about to get interesting.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.100
Lou!

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:30.230
What the hell?

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.740
Is Lou out of the picture?

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.370
Lou! Wait! I wasn't trying
to steal your shears!

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.500
I'm, um... so glad... you're all right!

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:59.260
Has my face been harmed?

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.810
I can't tell when you're that close.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.600
You look fine.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.110
Then let's go.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:14.980
Do you have any feelings at all?

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.070
She ignored me!

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.660
I'm amazed you didn't fall off that cliff.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.290
I grabbed a vine and hung on.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.000
You're bleeding. Doesn't it hurt?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.790
It hurts.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.750
Wait.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.590
Sit.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.970
There. That should do it.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:42.680
Seeing you all bloodied was repulsive.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.890
You're concerned for me?

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.810
Don't flatter yourself!

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:50.770
The only one I'm worried
about is Master Patrick.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:55.190
I imagine he's feeling quite anxious.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.030
Damn it. What is this place?

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:06.830
How dare you coop Patrick up like this?
You'll pay for this, Edward.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.380
Ricky, get over here, already.
Come to the rescue.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.210
You will come, won't you?

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:20.300
What is Patrick supposed
to do without you?

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.970
Somebody open up this damn thing!

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:27.510
Enough! This is absurd!
Don't keep Patrick cooped up like this!

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:31.270
This is no way to treat a shadow!

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.480
Please. This is unbearable.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.610
Ricky. Ricky...

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.650
Master Patrick?

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:46.410
Is that your voice I hear?

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.620
Don't worry. I'll help you.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.170
Good day, Master Patrick. Can you see me?

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:58.880
I don't think he can see you
with your eye pressed so close.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.550
Oh, really?

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:06.390
You're... Sunshine? Emilico, was it?

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.850
That's me!

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:14.390
Wait, did you hear what Patrick
was saying a moment ago?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.520
Yes. I'm sorry, but I heard what you said.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.820
This is absurd! Patrick doesn't
get rescued out of pity!

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.990
And especially not by a failure like you!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.910
Get out of here!
No one makes a fool of Patrick!

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:28.120
I'm not!

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.200
Liar! How could you not be?!

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.500
I said I'm not!

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.710
Put a cork in it! Go away, already!

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:37.000
I can't do that!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.260
No one would wish to be
left all alone in such a place.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:46.800
I never imagined that a shadow master
would be confined like this.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.930
I'm worried about Mistress Kate.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:54.810
And Ricky is worried
about you, Master Patrick.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:57.810
I know! I'll catch you up about Ricky.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:02.190
Edward read us a rule that said no harm
must come to a living doll's face.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:05.240
So Ricky chose a soot suit
to protect his face.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.410
He's really using his brain.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:11.450
Oh, and a shadow's attire
must not get dirty.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.910
You must take care, Master Patrick.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:18.500
Let's see. The crate is locked,
and there's a single air hole.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.090
Are there any hints about opening it?

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:25.340
You won't pass the
test if you help Patrick.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:28.890
How can I fail for helping?
As long as I'm being of service,

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:32.010
I'm more than happy!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:35.430
Enough. Hurry up and go find Kate.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:36.520
Huh?! But--

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.060
Save your scorn!

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:42.270
Ricky will be the one to save Patrick!
He <i>will </i>come.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:46.610
Besides, it will look bad
if Patrick doesn't wait.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:51.200
I almost stole Ricky's
chance to do his job.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:55.790
Well, please at least accept
what I drop through the hole.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.380
What's this?

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:04.590
An orange. It will boost your energy.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:07.630
Here's one more thing.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.550
It's a pretty flower I picked on the way.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:14.470
It will help the time fly
if you look at it.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.770
Goodbye.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:27.990
Next time, I look forward to
seeing you along with Mistress Kate.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:35.870
A flower? Sunshine really is
the perfect nickname for her.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:52.850
A heavy door? That's some
pretty plain-vanilla abuse.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:54.810
Shaun!

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.390
Emilico!

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.140
Three of the dolls have
come together here.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.690
Shaun certainly looks promising.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:05.070
If Dorothy were Sunshine,
she'd use him to her advantage.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:08.280
Sunshine does not think like that.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.360
If Ryan were Shaun,

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:15.490
he would use that heavy door
to trap and eliminate them.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:18.580
Then again, trapping them
would be a waste.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:22.420
Their looks of despair
would truly be a sight to see!

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.710
What a creep.

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:28.380
Have you not read their profiles?
The three of them are fast friends.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.470
And neither of you is Shaun or Emilico.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:36.720
This is what makes those two so unlikable.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.350
Something is written under the dots
marking the shadow masters' locations.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.560
But I can't see very well.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.150
Can you read it?

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:47.780
This isn't writing!

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.610
It's not?

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:50.740
It looks like a line.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.860
No one can write that small.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.530
That's true.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.870
Let's share our routes so far.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.330
The black dots caught my eye,

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:03.370
but I wanted to join up
with you first, so I came here.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:06.790
Wouldn't you rather investigate
that explosion together?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.960
This dot is Master Patrick.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.130
I think the explosion was here,
where there's a shadow master.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.840
I saw it from high up.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.140
I suspected as much.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.850
It has me worried,
so let's head there next.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.100
Sounds good.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:23.440
If we want the shortest route
through the labyrinth,

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:27.650
we'll have to pass through
the area we are in now.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:32.440
Another head-scratcher.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.530
It's not on the map.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:38.370
And there's no way to open these bars.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.990
Can't you climb over the wall?

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:44.830
No, the trees on the
other side are full of thorns.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.170
Plus, we found each other.
Let's finish this together.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:50.460
Thank you so much!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:11:00.810
There's something
about these animal statues.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:03.730
There's a gap at the base.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.480
It turns!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.530
Muddy water!

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.110
Now that's a stupid trap.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:19.450
Forgive me, Shaun!
I didn't mean to get you dirty!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.080
Don't worry.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.620
Now we know the statues move.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.830
I bet one of them is a
switch for opening the bars.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:29.710
But the others could be more traps.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:33.420
There might even be one
that harms your face.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.630
Maybe we should take the long way through.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.720
You're overthinking things, Shaun.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:43.390
Let's relax on this bench
and eat an orange!

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:47.140
You'll never change.
Is that from the greenhouse?

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.310
That's a lot of stuff.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.520
It will be hard to push uphill.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.860
We already did.

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:57.320
The weight from sitting...

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.610
That's it!

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:02.200
The statues are a diversion.
The bench is the switch!

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:06.370
And it's built for three.
Let's all sit down!

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:12.290
Nothing happened!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:15.710
Oh, right. Masters
and dolls come in pairs.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.970
There's no need for a three-seater.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.180
F-Forgive me.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:22.510
It was Shaun's idea for
the three of us to sit.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:26.390
Oh, um... Benches such as
these are often found in gardens.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.770
They are placed for
viewing special scenery.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.770
The view here <i>is </i>quite nice!

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:36.610
The way those trees overlap
makes them look like a rabbit!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.780
Let's go!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:50.250
What in the world happened?

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.250
Soot.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.460
There are footprints here.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.130
Whose could they be?

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.510
Master John.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.340
Let's follow them!

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.390
Was he caught in a trap?
Who would do such a thing?

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.270
Master John!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:16.150
It's hard to see around here,
and the footprints are gone.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:18.940
He's moving on his own,
so he must be fine!

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.740
Maybe he's on a walk!

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:26.330
You're right. That sounds like
something Master John would do.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:27.830
A phantom!

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:31.210
No, it's just a folly.
Don't scare me like that.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:32.290
What's a folly?

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:36.880
A structure or other feature placed
in a garden for decorative purposes.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:40.220
They can even be hideous.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:43.640
It's huge! I'm going to climb up!

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.470
Go ahead. I'll devise a plan.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.680
Okay!

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.180
If Master John is on a walk,
he'll be hard to find.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:54.440
With this terrain, we could
nearly cross paths and not notice.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.650
Maybe we should split up and search.

00:13:56.650 --> 00:14:00.190
It's Emilico from the beast's hair!

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:06.330
I started out so close to Master John,
but I was so bent on solving riddles

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:08.410
that I ended up heading
in Emilico's direction.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.290
That's just like you, Shaun.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:15.380
Master John?!

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.590
Hi.

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.340
What are you doing up there?

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:23.050
What is John doing? This folly is
so big and perfect for climbing.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.550
I'm glad you're safe.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:28.510
How'd you get out of the crate?

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.430
Soot is quite remarkable.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:35.520
Or perhaps one could say,
John is quite remarkable.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:40.280
In short, it was like, wham, bang, kaboom!

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:44.240
Master John, you have
some amazing soot power, too!

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:45.780
Shaun?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:50.290
Master John, your clothes are...

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.950
A shadow's attire

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.660
must not

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.040
get dirty.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:58.250
What?! No one told John about that.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.300
Is there nothing we could do?

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.670
I don't know.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:05.510
Shadows emit soot that
slowly dirties their clothes.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:09.810
Putting someone like that
in such a confined space...

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.350
Damn you, Edward!

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:15.060
John's power will blow away
every speck of soot!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.810
Master John, you'll just make it worse!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:22.110
Depriving one of such information
results in a huge disadvantage!

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:25.650
John must go back and warn Kate!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.740
Did you see Mistress Kate?

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.950
John is aiming for the top!

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:35.040
What?

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:40.090
In other words, the path that
goes uphill leads to Mistress Kate!

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:44.380
Emilico, why do you suddenly
understand everything Master John says?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:49.140
John had a word with Kate and...

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.520
What's the matter?!

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:55.180
Your fiancée?!

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.890
King of Shadows House?!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:59.980
Not another word!
John knows what you're thinking!

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.980
It sounds completely crazy.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.450
Blurting it all out like
that was not intentional!

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:10.030
But it can't be helped
when one is nervous.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:13.910
I never knew Master John lost
his inhibitions when nervous.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.660
Don't feel blue.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.580
Have an orange!

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.830
That's a map, not a napkin.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.840
Come to think of it, you're Kate's face.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.050
Yes, sir!

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:26.300
Don't tell her what you just heard.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:27.590
Yes, sir!

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.680
Here you are.

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:40.270
You're adorable, like a little sister,
but a bit too childish for Kate's face.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:43.940
Then again, John fell
for what's inside of Kate.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:45.900
Plus, she has fine soot.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:50.160
And you can tell how beautiful
her heart is by looking at her face.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:53.660
The face one cultivates
reflects one's self.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:57.870
That means Kate must have
an adorable side just like you.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.750
Nobility and sweetness all in one package!

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.630
But enough about that.

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.920
Emilico, it won't be easy saving Kate.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.220
Huh?

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:15.850
Oh, I see. Mistress Kate is
in a frightening predicament.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.890
Surely you'll think of something.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:20.980
You're a fine face.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.940
Shaun, may I borrow your magnifying glass?

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.940
I will check the route to Mistress Kate.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.990
It's too dark here.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.280
Rum, may I borrow your lantern?

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.870
Mm-hmm.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:38.700
Magnifying glasses are so much fun!

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.250
Oh, an ant just crawled onto the map!

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:42.750
Stop playing around.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:47.420
She's far too optimistic,
but it's one of her charms.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:52.180
You know that writing you thought
was under the dots? I figured it out.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:56.720
I thought it was a single line,
but a closer look reveals dashes.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:01.060
It's a code for the rankings
we received in the debut hall.

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:03.310
Here's Master John...

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:05.440
Master Patrick...

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.690
Mistress Louise...

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.940
Mistress Shirley...

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.700
and Mistress Kate!

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:14.910
Now we know where each shadow master is!

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:18.910
Isn't that wonderful, Rum?
Mistress Shirley is close by.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:23.500
I held the map too close,
and it started to burn!

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.750
But what an interesting pattern!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:29.510
There are scorches where
the orange juice dripped.

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:33.300
There are other strange
scorches like this one.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.470
Let's try my map, too.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.680
Try John's, too.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.520
Master John?!

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:44.020
Nice work, Rum!

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:48.190
The dark areas that appear are...

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:53.150
Elevation! This will help figure out
how the paths are connected!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.910
You're amazing, Shaun!

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:59.200
We should check the sootglass
to see how much time is left.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:02.410
Sootglass, sootglass...

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.830
There's 50 minutes left.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:12.340
"Based on the amount of soot in the
sootglass and the distance walked..."

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.970
Forget the sootglass.
She calculated the time!

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:18.050
Wow. Who knew you could do that?

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.600
Now then...

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:23.600
What shall we do with Master John's
soot-stained clothes?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.650
Maybe there's a change
of clothes near the exit.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:29.190
Besides, is it really that bad?

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:30.940
You're filthy.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.860
What a royal pain.
John is going to clobber Edward!

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.820
Wait a moment.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.240
I think I figured it out.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.370
Look at this.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:41.240
There's no soot there!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.370
Let's go have a look, Shaun.

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:44.290
Yes, sir.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:49.380
But we can't see the rest of
the information on your map.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:58.930
She said she's memorized
the map, so you can have hers.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:01.010
The whole map? Really?!

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:02.720
Thanks, Rum.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.890
One more thing.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:08.310
About the path that leads to Kate...

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:10.440
The bridge John crossed to get there

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:11.480
collapsed.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.400
What?!

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.990
There was a warning
written in front of it.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:17.400
It said, "Two crossings only."

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:20.910
The only way now is
that dreadful maze below.

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:23.200
I'm getting dizzy just looking at it.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:27.330
All your wandering has complicated things.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.880
Shaun, you've adopted a rather
casual tone toward your master.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:33.420
F-Forgive me.

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:34.920
No.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.970
It's perfect.

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:40.930
There's only one path on the
lower level that leads to the exit.

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:43.010
So it's Mistress Kate,

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.140
Mistress Shirley,

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:45.520
and then the exit.

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:47.940
That's the only route from here.

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:53.020
No, we should use this path on the
right to head back the way you came.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:56.280
The path to Mistress Kate
looks kind of hard.

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:58.450
I want to help you.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:00.910
You already did.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.990
You noticed the lines below the dots.

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:07.330
And you told me how
benches are used in gardens.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:13.000
I wouldn't have noticed the rabbit unless
you had told me about viewing the scenery.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:19.050
I've gotten this far thanks
to you, Rum, and Master John.

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:22.180
Each doll must save their own master.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:25.350
That's what Master Patrick told me.

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:29.270
Shaun, you must be
the one to save Master John!

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:35.650
You're right.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.990
Well, Emilico, this is where we part ways.

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:40.110
All right.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:45.410
Rum, at first I thought you were
all wishy-washy and helpless.

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:49.830
But I was wrong. You're quite
capable, and you've got guts.

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:05.050
May we all make it through
the debut and meet once more!

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:28.370
<i>No ash, no, just shadow</i>

00:22:28.370 --> 00:22:32.750
<i>A no-"I" body, like a dolly</i>

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:36.670
<i>I'm hollow, where'd I go?</i>

00:22:36.670 --> 00:22:39.460
<i>Nobody knows</i>

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:43.840
<i>A murky "I" with black-hole eyes</i>

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:47.510
<i>A mimic, oh my! I'm in disguise?</i>

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.060
<i>"Thank you"? Thank who?</i>

00:22:50.060 --> 00:22:53.690
<i>Every answer is true</i>

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:57.310
<i>If I am no one</i>

00:22:57.310 --> 00:23:01.190
<i>And I can do nothing</i>

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:04.780
<i>Is it a waste to keep living?</i>

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:08.160
<i>Is it wrong to go on?</i>

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:13.080
<i>What's missing here is me, me, me</i>

00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:15.670
<i>Without a self</i>

00:23:15.670 --> 00:23:20.250
<i>Swept away before anyone see, see, sees</i>

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:23.090
<i>Like dust from the shelf</i>

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:27.640
<i>Neither happy nor sad</i>

00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:30.470
<i>Don't feel good or bad</i>

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:32.520
<i>Not up to snuff</i>

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:38.060
<i>I can't even bluff</i>

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:41.780
<i>Would you believe this stuff?</i>

